(value 5 (shen-jit.lower.prim-arity shen-jit.copy-bytes))
(value -1 (shen-jit.lower.prim-arity if))
(value -1 (shen-jit.lower.prim-arity fixed-nothing))
(value true (shen-jit.lower.fixed? if))
(value true (shen-jit.lower.fixed? protect))
(value true (shen-jit.lower.fixed? cons))
(value false (shen-jit.lower.fixed? fixed-nothing))
(value false (shen-jit.lower.fixed? 5))
"Rewrites in the lowerer keep scope and order when the code is not the kernel's usual shape."
"Nested lambdas that bind one name twice: the inner binding wins, called with both arguments at once."
(value 2 (let F (if true (lambda X (lambda X X)) 0) (F 1 2)))
"A condition that binds a name the then branch uses for something else: sharing its selectors would capture it."
(value t.lower-share (defun t.lower-share (X P) (if (let X (hd P) true) (cons X (cons (hd P) ())) 0)))
(value (99 1) (t.lower-share 99 (cons 1 ())))
"Dereferences compared at once only when the second argument cannot change the bindings."
(value 100 (set shen.*prolog-memory* 100))
(value false (let B (shen.prolog-vector) (let X (shen.newpv B) (do (shen.bindv X 1 B) (= (shen.deref X B) (shen.deref (do (shen.bindv X 2 B) 2) B))))))
"A query whose freeze is not a continuation keeps its vector of bindings, which the freeze may read later."
(value 2 (let F (((((lambda B (lambda L (lambda K (lambda C (freeze (<-address B 1)))))) (shen.prolog-vector)) 0) 0) 0) (let B2 (shen.prolog-vector) (do (address-> B2 1 99) (thaw F)))))
"A query's lock, key and continuation are evaluated outside its own variables."
(value true (let B 7 (((((lambda B (lambda L (lambda K (lambda C (number? L))))) (shen.prolog-vector)) B) 0) 0)))
"Inlined sealed bodies: a parameter bound again, a literal shaped like lowered code, and a parameter named lambda."
(value true (shen-jit.sealing true))
(value t.lower-frozen (defun t.lower-frozen (P) (let P (freeze 2) (thaw P))))
(value t.lower-literal (defun t.lower-literal () (cons apply (cons (cons var (cons T ())) ()))))
(value t.lower-keyword (defun t.lower-keyword (lambda X) (lambda X X)))
(value false (shen-jit.sealing false))
(value 2 (t.lower-frozen (freeze 1)))
(value (apply (var T)) (let T (freeze 7) (t.lower-literal)))
(value (7 7) (t.lower-keyword (lambda A (lambda B (cons A (cons B ())))) 7))
"The lowerer's tree walkers visit a node's parts, not its tail as if it were a node, so parameters named
like the lowerer's own node tags (apply, var) are variables like any other."
(value (const 7) (let F (let G (freeze (cons const (cons 7 ()))) (lambda apply G)) (thaw (F 0))))
(value 7 (let X 7 (let G (freeze (lambda var X)) (let X 99 ((thaw G) 0)))))
(value "boom" (let F (trap-error (simple-error "boom") (lambda E (lambda var E))) (error-to-string (F 0))))
(value t.walk-capture (defun t.walk-capture (X) (do (cons X (cons X (cons X (cons X ())))) (t.walk-target 99 (lambda var X)))))
(value t.walk-target (defun t.walk-target (A F) (F 0)))
(value 7 (t.walk-capture 7))
